# Docker build context for the oneiro-ostis machine image.
#
# Measured 2026-10-02: with no .dockerignore the context was 6.02 GB in 61,095
# files, of which worktrees/ alone was 5.67 GB. The machine build never reads
# that directory - Docker was packing it anyway. After these rules the context
# is a few tens of MB of actual sources.
#
# Everything the C++ build reads is kept: CMakeLists.txt, CMakePresets.json,
# cmake/, problem-solver/, requirements.txt and scripts/. The image produces
# everything else itself.

# Four git worktrees of the PARENT workspace repo (.git/worktrees/oneiro-live-tg*),
# checked out by an unrelated Telegram session and still registered with that
# repository. They are another agent's working copies, not build inputs.
worktrees/

# Build outputs the image regenerates for itself: cmake --preset release writes
# build/Release, install_cxx_problem_solver.sh downloads sc-machine into
# install/sc-machine. Excluding install/ also stops a stale host copy from
# overlaying the freshly downloaded one when the builder stage runs COPY . .
build/
install/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Local virtualenv and tool caches.
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# .runtime/ is this project's own diagnostic area: graph snapshots, scratch
# graph copies and probe scripts. 73 MB of evidence, not build inputs.
.runtime/

# Live graph storage. The deployment mounts the named volume kb-binary at
# /kb.bin and never reads this directory, and a graph must never be baked into
# an image where a rebuild would silently carry a stale copy forward.
kb.bin/

# Runtime state and server logs.
logs/
state/

# Repository history is not a build input.
.git/